doc: requirements.hick
83e1|<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
fc06|<hick:doc xmlns:hick="http://www.hickorydocs.com/1.0" weave="requirements.md">
328e|# Todo app — requirements
f011|
fd80|<hick:upstream file="domain.hick" />
f011|
c83e|One edge declared. The glossary comes from the domain model one hop up, and
122e|the decisions come from the kickoff meeting **two** hops up — this document
a807|never names the meeting, and does not have to. Change a decision in the
fc8f|meeting notes and this document, its tickets, and the domain model all go
1fea|stale together.
f011|
b097|## Vocabulary in force
f011|
1dfd|<hick:paste select=".glossary" />
f011|
043b|## Decisions in force
f011|
dff3|<hick:paste select=".decision" />
f011|
211a|## Requirements
f011|
fde9|Each requirement below is also a ticket. The ticket files under `work/` are
c80d|tangled from these fragments — the requirement and the ticket are the same
4a47|bytes, so they cannot drift. Editing the requirement IS editing the ticket.
f011|
98c5|<hick:copy id="r-add">
b92d|`todo add "<title>"` creates an open task and prints its id. The id is short,
85e9|opaque, and assigned at creation; it is never derived from the title.
ae0e|</hick:copy>
f011|
2075|<hick:copy id="r-list">
6010|`todo list` prints every task in creation order as `<id> <state> <title>`.
3d2e|Dropped tasks are included — retaining them is pointless if the default view
e53b|hides them. `--state open|done|dropped` filters.
ae0e|</hick:copy>
f011|
6d79|<hick:copy id="r-done">
b81a|`todo done <id>` moves a task to done. `todo drop <id>` moves it to dropped.
0049|Both are idempotent: re-running on a task already in that state succeeds and
d788|changes nothing, so a retried command is never an error.
ae0e|</hick:copy>
f011|
b2d8|<hick:copy id="r-storage">
4826|Tasks persist to `tasks.json` in the working directory, created on first
24cb|write. A missing file reads as an empty list, not an error — the first run of
a00b|a fresh install must behave like every later run.
ae0e|</hick:copy>
f011|
471e|<hick:copy id="r-rename">
d792|`todo rename <id> "<new title>"` changes a task's title, leaving its id and
971b|state untouched. This is the requirement the opaque-id decision exists for:
8af0|anything referencing a task must survive a retitle. An unknown id exits
20f3|nonzero, like the other commands that take one.
ae0e|</hick:copy>
f011|
