83e1|<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
0d8f|<hick:doc xmlns:hick="http://www.hickorydocs.com/1.0" weave="2026-08-07-kickoff.md">
0ff7|# Todo app — kickoff, 7 Aug 2026
f011|
f488|Raw notes. This is the top of the chain: everything downstream reaches these
b4ee|decisions by reference, so a decision is written down exactly once and the
6d0f|documents that depend on it fail when it changes.
f011|
e592|Present: Nate. Notes taken live.
f011|
5d87|## What we're building
f011|
6535|A todo app. Deliberately small — it exists to exercise the whole lifecycle,
3008|meeting through shipped code, not to be a product.
f011|
dbec|## Decisions
f011|
477e|Pasted back into these notes deliberately. `hick:copy` blocks are EXTRACTED,
346c|not rendered — without this the notes weave to an empty section, and the one
3ff2|document where a decision is actually written down becomes the one document
6b7e|you cannot read it in. It also makes this document's own drift check
1727|meaningful: change a decision and these notes go stale too, not just the
cea7|documents downstream.
f011|
dff3|<hick:paste select=".decision" />
f011|
79d8|<hick:copy id="d-storage" class="decision">
20fa|Tasks persist to a single JSON file on disk. No database. The app must run
40c1|with no service dependencies, because the point is to exercise the document
54dc|chain, not an install.
ae0e|</hick:copy>
f011|
1778|<hick:copy id="d-states" class="decision">
cb92|A task is in exactly one of three states: **open**, **done**, or
c028|**dropped**. Dropped is not deleted — it stays in the file and stays
33a4|listable, because "what did we decide not to do" is the question people
4eaa|actually come back for.
ae0e|</hick:copy>
f011|
edfb|<hick:copy id="d-identity" class="decision">
85c1|Tasks are identified by a short opaque id assigned on creation, never by
9391|their title. Titles are editable; anything that references a task must
e547|survive a retitle.
ae0e|</hick:copy>
f011|
1488|<hick:copy id="d-interface" class="decision">
38ef|The interface is a CLI. No web UI in the first cut — a UI would double the
32bc|surface without exercising any part of the lifecycle that the CLI does not.
ae0e|</hick:copy>
f011|
c39b|## Open questions
f011|
40ff|Not decisions yet, deliberately left loose:
f011|
6129|- Does a task need a due date? Nobody argued for it. Left out.
a8e3|- Sub-tasks? Same. If it comes up twice, it becomes a decision.
f011|
4427|## Not discussed
f011|
4975|Multi-user, sync, auth. Out of scope for the first cut.
de5c|</hick:doc>

